[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: scribe move renames on disk outside Graph, pending and save

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-MOVE-BYPASSES-THE-MODEL
TITLE: scribe move renames on disk outside Graph, pending and save
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
scribe move resolves its destination through scribe_verbs.target_path, then scribe_ops._move makes the daemon-held document pass the same render-and-reparse boundary used by writes. A dry run reports the rename and discards speculative state. A real move renames the file, discards the held generation, and forces the next read to reload it. The final filesystem rename does not pass through Graph.save, but it no longer bypasses document validation or leave the resident graph pretending the source path still exists.
<<<
